This file exists only so the frontend/public directory is tracked by
git (git does not track empty directories). The frontend Dockerfile's
runner stage does `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public`, which is
the standard Next.js standalone-output pattern - it fails outright if
the directory doesn't exist at all, which is what broke build-frontend
in Cloud Build (build dc7b607e's frontend step / build 1982477c).
